WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Good afternoon ladies and gentlemen and welcome to each of you and all of you to the second presentation in this year's Solomon Goldman Lecture Series.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
I'm Byron Sherwin, Vice President of Spertus College.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:31.340
The Solomon Goldman Lecture Series has been endowed in perpetuity in memory of the late Rabbi Solomon Goldman of Anshanet Synagogue here in Chicago.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:38.320
This year, we are focusing the Solomon Goldman Lecture Series on great Jewish books.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:46.320
Last month, we heard Professor Lawrence Fine of Indiana University talk to us about the Zohar.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:57.140
Today we will hear our own Professor Jose Faor talk to us about Joseph Caro and his great masterpiece of Jewish law, the Shulchan Aruch.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:06.560
We also today join in the worldwide commemoration this year of the 500th anniversary of the birth of Joseph Caro.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:16.040
And in that regard, I want particularly to welcome those of you who are here who claim descent from Joseph Caro.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:26.940
There are few people in the world as qualified to speak about Joseph Caro as the Ezra Senzibar professor at Spurtus College, Jose Faor.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:36.160
Last March, when he delivered his first lecture at the college, Dr. Faor was a stranger to our college and to our city.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:45.540
Now he is almost part of our institutional family, and I know that many of you here have attended his classes and public lectures during the past year.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:53.100
Two of Dr. Faor's most prominent areas of interest are Sephardic Jewry and Jewish Law,

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:57.060
and these two areas coalesce in the person of Joseph Caro.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:03.960
I am therefore pleased and honored to present Yosef Faor, who will speak about Yosef Caro.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.240
Thank you, Dr. Sherwin.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:23.800
Ladies and gentlemen, we will be examining the life, works, and ideas of perhaps the most influential Jew in the last 450 years.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.500
Joseph Caro was born in Toledo.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:38.560
He left Spain in 1492 when he was about five years old, and he died at the age of 87 in Safed, Israel.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:49.940
The place of birth, Toledo, symbolizes one of the most important essential elements in the vision of Joseph Caro.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:53.560
Toledo was a cosmopolitan city.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:03:02.340
It was the only city in Spain that embraced both the Muslim Moorish tradition on the one hand

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:09.220
and the Catholic European ideas and ideals on the other.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:15.800
Jews in Toledo spoke both Arabic and Spanish for centuries.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.800
the school of Toledo of Jews

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.900
was

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.160
the translator

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:24.300
of most of the

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.520
Arabic classics that passed from

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.080
the Arabic into Hebrew

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.740
and from the Hebrew into Latin

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.740
so Arabic was a very important

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.560
element in the

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.560
life of Toledo

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.860
as a matter of fact

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.280
the name Karo

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.600
symbolizes the passing from the Arabic

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:43.860
culture into the

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.620
European culture

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.320
in several of his writings

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.500
Joseph Caro points out

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.900
that Israel's family name was Habib

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.460
and Caro

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.440
means beloved

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.520
it's just the Spanish translation

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.700
of a very very famous name

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:00.540
Habib

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.240
now later on

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.320
his vision

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.440
of biculturalism

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.540
Muslim Jews

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.620
in Muslim lands

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.840
and Jews in European lands

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.140
this was the vision that he

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:17.900
grew with in Toledo

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:21.160
becomes one of the essential elements

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.960
in his Shulchan Aruch, in his code of Jewish law.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.780
I will just say a few details of his life.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.160
Details that are terribly important.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.900
He was, in a sense, besides a legalist,

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.220
he was a kind of a mystic.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.180
And there is a story.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.580
The story happened to be authentic.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:43.440
And it's so fantastic

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:49.740
that if not because of documentation, we would put the story into the realm of fable.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:57.320
Joseph Carroll tells in one of his autobiographical books called Magit Mereşit,

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:03.900
in which he records his mystic visions, how when he was in Andrianople in Turkey

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:08.320
and later on when he was in Saloniki, also was part of the Ottoman Empire,

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:16.720
He was always, always in search of independent economic means by which he could study Torah

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:23.020
and not depend either on the salary of a community or on business.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:30.000
And for years and years struggled towards that aim without any success.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:36.160
He fully tells that he decided to go into business and he went into a partnership.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:39.120
but because he would not come on time

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.900
engaged in the study of Talmud

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.780
the partnership was broken

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.200
he didn't know what to do

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.240
he goes into the market

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.240
and a strange man

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:55.660
tall, with features that he never saw before

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.580
but somehow inspired him

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:02.000
confidence, he tells him that he has a mortar

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.920
that he wants to sell the mortar

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.540
Joseph Culler didn't understand much about metals

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.100
and he says, well

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:12.820
I buy this mortar from you

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:14.300
what should be the price?

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.500
and the man says, how much money are you carrying with you?

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.460
and he gave him the money

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:22.680
he goes back to his house

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:26.080
and he brings this mortar to his wife

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.780
it was an old mortar

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.680
nothing to do with it

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:33.640
he goes to the school

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:34.880
and his wife

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.500
tries to find somebody

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.860
who understands about metals

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:41.160
that maybe they could give him an idea

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:42.120
what to do with the mortar.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.580
The mortar turned to be

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:47.260
a mortar made of solid gold.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:49.300
Eventually,

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.520
he sells this mortar

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:52.980
and with the money,

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:55.100
he establishes himself

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.820
in the city of Safed

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:59.380
and he's able to publish

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:01.340
all of his masterpieces

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:02.860
including the Bet Yosef,

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:10.140
the Shukran Aruch, all of them were published with the money that came out, the result of this mortar.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:15.480
He further tells the following story, that the man who sold them the mortar,

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:21.920
appears to him in a dream, and says, I am you, I am your destiny, I am your faith,

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.860
and I was just facilitating to you what you always wanted.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:30.840
I want to tell another aspect

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.200
of his life

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:33.260
that was very important

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:35.360
and moved him to go to Israel

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:37.480
and that was

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:40.380
that a famous Jew

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:42.140
by the name of Shlomo Molho

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:43.780
who happened to have been

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:46.220
the secretary to the king of Portugal

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:48.340
happened realizing

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:49.540
his Jewishness

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:51.180
he circumcises himself

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:53.540
escapes from Lisbon

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:55.320
goes into Europe

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:58.080
starts studying and preaching Kabbalah

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.200
and eventually is burnt alive

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:03.500
by the Inquisition.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:06.860
Joseph Caro envied that man

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.380
and he thought that these conversos

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.000
with their own behavior

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.620
of the Kiddush Hashem

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:15.060
were doing something that in a sense

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:16.680
was far, far more important

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.080
than his telling of Torah.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.420
And inspired by the death of Shlomo Molho,

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.440
he decides to do something for the Jewish people.

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:29.300
And he devotes himself not only to study, but also to writing.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.520
Now we will analyze his Shulchan Aruch.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:38.060
But before, let me point out that there were other works that he did.

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:45.580
Joseph Caro is the author of an extraordinary handbook,

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:49.560
Methodologies of the Talmud.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:53.160
in which he gives very short

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:55.660
but very profound rules

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:58.980
concerning interpretation of the Talmud.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:00.580
This is one of the works.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.020
He also has another book

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:06.580
that is a collection of very brief notes

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:10.180
on the Pentateuch and other books of the Bible

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:14.320
that he used for his own private homilies.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:17.240
There is a third book

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:20.800
which is the Kesef Mishneh for thick volumes

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.280
that is the second best interpretation

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:27.360
to Maimonides' famous code, Mishneh Torah.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:33.360
In addition, he published two volumes of Rispansa.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:37.720
One volume devoted entirely to Jewish family law

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:41.100
and that's called Shalot Uchivot Maran Bet Yosef

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.120
and another volume, Avkat Rohel

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:47.000
dealing with variety of Jewish rituals

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.620
and Jewish monetary cases.

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:55.860
Furthermore, as I mentioned before, there are the notes, biographical notes,

00:09:56.200 --> 00:10:02.200
Magit Mesharrim, which are mystical insights, mystical visions that he entertained,

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:05.940
part of which, and only part of which, are now published.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:13.700
His true intellectual career began with the Bet Yosef.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:19.620
Now, Debut Yosef is a milestone in Jewish intellectual history.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:21.300
Why?

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:24.540
Formally, it is a commentary.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:28.220
It is a commentary on a book written in Spain, in Toledo,

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.980
by the famous Yaakov Ben Asher,

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:38.600
one of the great luminary individuals coming from Germany,

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:39.900
settling in Toledo.

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:41.680
He writes a commentary.

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:45.220
but in truth, debate yourself is not a commentary

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:47.360
it is something which both

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:49.840
best transcends

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:51.900
and shows the whole

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:55.500
Jewish legal tradition

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:59.220
beyond and behind the tour

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:03.120
there are some very important ideas

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:05.520
which will determine forever

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:07.840
the cause of Jewish legal development

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:10.060
and these are the following

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:26.400
Number one, whereas in Ashkenazic tradition, dialectics, pilpul, the analysis of the text was the determining factor,

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:36.860
Joseph Carroll believed that in law, dialectics should play a very minor role.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:43.000
that law should be decided on the basis of authority.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:48.740
Not dialectics, but authority.

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:52.940
Now, what determines authority?

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:57.620
And here again, there are two very important insights.

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:03.700
Number one, the acceptability of the community.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:15.960
A scholar is considered authoritative not only because of his legal analysis or his legal knowledge,

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:25.540
but essentially when and if and how much of the Jewish community accepts his rulings.

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:43.500
It is the acceptability of the jurist by the community and that alone that will establish the authorities and the limits of a POSEC, a Jewish-Jewish consult.

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:55.260
This is totally revolutionary because normally both in Jewish and non-Jewish tradition, a legal authority is imposed on the public.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:13:01.360
It is imposed either by the political system or by the religious system.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:06.320
But it is always an authority that is imposed on the public.

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:14.780
Joseph Kano discovered that we cannot impose a Jewish authority on the Jewish public.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.880
It is rather the other way around.

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:30.740
The Jewish public will choose that posse or legal writer that they recognize as authoritative.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:38.680
In this area, Joseph Caro establishes a new idea.

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:45.980
The interrelationship between Jewish scholarship and the Jewish community.

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:47.160
This is one point.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:14:06.060
Second point, ideally, following Jewish judiciary tradition, no one single individual should decide on his own what the law is.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:13.180
As a matter of fact, we have the concept of a bedin, a tribunal.

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:15.780
the minimum tribunal

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:17.700
must constitute

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:19.500
at least three judges

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:22.040
and this is grounded

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.380
on the whole notion

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.340
the biblical idea

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.020
that no individual

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:26.720
alone

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:28.780
could perceive the whole truth

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:30.960
now

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:33.060
we were in need therefore

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:35.240
of at least

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:37.860
three judges

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:40.480
where to find

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:41.500
these three judges

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:45.080
how can we find three judges

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:47.220
that on the one hand

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:50.380
will be accepted by the whole Jewish community

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:52.340
or the majority of the entire Jewish community

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:54.220
furthermore

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:56.020
that these judges

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:58.620
will last forever

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:00.720
because we cannot go

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:03.460
and undergo the same process

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:05.420
generation after generation

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:07.600
and finally

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:09.040
and finally

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:12.140
that they should have the imprimatur,

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:13.880
the seal,

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.280
of Talmudic authority.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:21.000
How to find that kind of a tribunal?

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:25.480
Now, an event took place

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:29.980
while Joseph Caro was in Israel, in Safed.

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:35.100
And that event is going to be transformed by Joseph Caro

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:36.900
into the Shulchan Aruch.

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:38.860
Let me tell you what the event was.

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:53.040
Jews upon leaving Spain, they were almost in a parallel situation to that of the Jews leaving Auschwitz 40 years ago.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:16:01.040
They were totally demoralized. Many of them, or majority of them, had been victims of the Inquisitions.

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:18.040
Many of them had seen their brothers, sisters, fathers, mothers burnt alive at the stake, totally depossessed, humiliated, no books, no honor, no dignity.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:30.040
They were scattered throughout the four corners of the world, from Goa in the east, in Asia, to the Americas in the west.

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:46.060
There was a demoralization. Many of them turned into mysticism. A mysticism that eventually would degenerate into the Shabbatai Tzvi movement. Others became skeptics. Others, libertines.

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:49.380
Jacob Berav

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:52.740
who eventually became one of the teachers

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:55.280
of Maran Joseph Caro

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:58.560
decided that what was at need

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:00.860
was Jewish authority

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:03.560
somehow we have to go back

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:06.360
and establish Jewish authority

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:09.760
what the Inquisition had done in Spain

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:12.540
was to wound, to kill

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:16.260
to undermine any concept of Jewish authority.

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:19.240
There was Judaism, fine,

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:21.020
but there is no Jewish authority.

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:23.760
At best, Judaism could be an ideal,

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:26.020
but it is not an authority

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.660
because it is totally, absolutely powerless.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.000
Jacob Beraf,

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:37.040
studying very carefully Maimonides,

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:40.280
came to the following discovery.

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:44.120
according to Jewish tradition

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.240
legal tradition

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:47.980
if somebody would have

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:49.120
an ordination

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:51.000
a smicha

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.240
coming all the way

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:56.300
back to

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:56.940
Moses

00:17:56.940 --> 00:18:00.080
this individual

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:02.420
by the fact

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:04.540
of being a link

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.460
in the chain

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:08.240
of tradition going back all the way

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:09.040
to Moshe Rabbeinu

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:12.660
that person will have legal authority

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:16.560
to decide what Jewish law is.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.740
Now, this chain of tradition

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:23.580
has been broken already in Talmudic times.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:27.080
By studying Maimonides,

00:18:28.180 --> 00:18:30.280
Jacob Barav discovered the following.

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:33.560
That the Jewish people,

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:36.440
the Jewish community,

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:38.720
Am Yisrael,

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:46.080
have the power to bestow smicha to anyone that the community chooses.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:51.300
So that there is a political dimension to smicha.

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:55.140
You could be musmach because you represent Moses,

00:18:56.780 --> 00:19:01.280
or you could be musmach because you represent the Jewish people.

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:03.800
and thereupon

00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:07.020
Yaakov Beraf came with the idea

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:08.640
that we should have

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:10.300
Musma Hymn in our days

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:14.800
and through an extraordinary apparatus

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:15.760
of propaganda

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:18.460
changes public opinion

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.540
and it gets

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:22.760
about 13

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:23.980
individuals

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:29.060
that they are designated by the entire

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:29.860
Jewish community

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:32.360
as musmahim,

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:36.640
as legal representatives of the communities.

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:41.600
They began already with a tribunal.

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:43.900
In theory,

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:47.740
this tribunal could revise every single law,

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:51.380
including the law legislated in the Talmud.

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:55.720
And because this tribunal would be musmah,

00:19:55.720 --> 00:20:00.700
of the same legal status as that of the Talmud,

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:05.740
in theory, it could revise, upset, change,

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:07.680
including the decisions of the Talmud.

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:13.720
The project was opposed by one single individual,

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:15.820
Rabbi Levib and Habib.

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:20.680
By the way, the Habib, as I said, was the Hebrew name of the Karo.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:23.880
He opposed the project.

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:28.180
eventually the dream of Yaakov Beraf

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:31.660
of establishing an autonomous Jewish Supreme Court

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:34.240
came to naught

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:37.360
the Turkish authorities

00:20:37.360 --> 00:20:39.800
probably alerted by the Jewish people

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:43.240
saw in this kind of a Bedin

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:47.500
a political dimension

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:51.660
that was unacceptable to the Ottoman Empire

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:54.280
Yaakov Beraf had to escape

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:56.180
and he went to Damascus

00:20:56.180 --> 00:20:58.180
he died eventually he dies in Damascus

00:20:58.180 --> 00:21:00.100
now

00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:01.080
Joseph Caro

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:03.580
has

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:05.080
a change

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:08.240
of the program he changes the program

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:09.260
he changes the vision

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:12.040
he says we could have a Bedin

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:14.780
but the Bedin

00:21:14.780 --> 00:21:15.820
should be composed

00:21:15.820 --> 00:21:18.660
of those people who are no longer

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:19.240
alive

00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:22.420
of dead judges.

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:24.520
How could you have it?

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:25.520
Very simple, he says.

00:21:26.420 --> 00:21:31.220
A judge is a judge by virtue of being accepted as such by the community.

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:34.520
And he pointed out very clearly

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:39.040
that the Jewish communities at the time were divided into three.

00:21:41.140 --> 00:21:44.260
You had in Europe the Ashkenazi, German communities.

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:51.960
and the greatest Jewish legal mind from Germany was the Roche,

00:21:52.140 --> 00:22:00.940
who came eventually, lived and taught and died in Toledo, the Roche.

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:08.800
So let's take his book, that would be one judge, the book of the Roche.

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:14.120
Second, there were the North African communities.

00:22:14.260 --> 00:22:25.620
Morocco, Algiers, Libya. And these communities were ruled by the famous Isaac Alfasi, the author of the Reef.

00:22:26.060 --> 00:22:36.120
That should be the second judge. And then you had the communities in the Near East, the communities from the south of Spain,

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:38.440
Andalusia, who ruled

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:40.360
themselves according to the book of

00:22:40.360 --> 00:22:42.020
Maimonides, the Mishneh Torah.

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:46.240
And Joseph Caro proposes taking

00:22:46.240 --> 00:22:47.220
these three books

00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:50.220
and turning these three books

00:22:50.220 --> 00:22:51.300
into a tribunal,

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:54.060
investigating

00:22:54.060 --> 00:22:55.280
every single issue.

00:22:56.740 --> 00:22:58.100
And in those issues

00:22:58.100 --> 00:22:59.760
in which these three

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:01.460
authorities agree,

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:03.400
the law should be like them.

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.020
If there is a dispute,

00:23:06.120 --> 00:23:11.780
like in all legal procedures, we follow the majority.

00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:16.180
And therefore we should follow two out of three.

00:23:17.820 --> 00:23:21.420
Now you would say, yes, but there is a flaw in this kind of legal thinking.

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:24.520
They were not technically musmahim.

00:23:25.940 --> 00:23:31.600
Nobody actually appointed them as the judges of Israel.

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:34.100
Although historically there were judges in Israel.

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:36.920
but the ceremony

00:23:36.920 --> 00:23:37.980
the smicha

00:23:37.980 --> 00:23:40.120
was not bestowed upon them

00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:42.740
and there Joseph Carroll

00:23:42.740 --> 00:23:43.820
comes with this idea and says

00:23:43.820 --> 00:23:46.720
and I in quality

00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:47.820
of musmach

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:50.880
will endorse

00:23:50.880 --> 00:23:53.380
the decision

00:23:53.380 --> 00:23:55.620
you have a tribunal

00:23:55.620 --> 00:23:58.520
representing the entire Jewish community

00:23:58.520 --> 00:24:03.240
you have a musmach

00:24:03.240 --> 00:24:06.980
writing the final legal decision.

00:24:08.080 --> 00:24:10.360
And this final legal decision

00:24:10.360 --> 00:24:12.800
becomes the Shulchan Aruch.

00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:17.240
I will explain later on what the Shulchan Aruch exactly means.

00:24:18.840 --> 00:24:20.940
Now, again,

00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:23.880
from the point of view of law,

00:24:25.720 --> 00:24:29.420
if an individual will follow the instructions of a judge,

00:24:30.080 --> 00:24:31.240
of a bona fide judge,

00:24:31.240 --> 00:24:34.640
no matter what professors of law may think

00:24:34.640 --> 00:24:40.260
the individual who follow that legal opinion

00:24:40.260 --> 00:24:42.220
the instructions of the judge

00:24:42.220 --> 00:24:47.340
he is within the spirit and the letter of the law

00:24:47.340 --> 00:24:51.800
and this is what Shukran Aruch is

00:24:51.800 --> 00:24:54.180
it is a legal code

00:24:54.180 --> 00:24:57.220
now any opinion

00:24:57.220 --> 00:24:59.780
contrary to Shukran Aruch

00:24:59.780 --> 00:25:02.780
could have intellectual merits.

00:25:04.100 --> 00:25:06.060
But from the point of view of law,

00:25:07.680 --> 00:25:09.520
the Shekharan Rukh is unshakable

00:25:09.520 --> 00:25:12.940
because the decision was written

00:25:12.940 --> 00:25:14.780
by Amusmach.

00:25:15.760 --> 00:25:18.560
Since the Smikha stopped

00:25:18.560 --> 00:25:22.860
with the death of Yaakov Beraf and Joseph Karo,

00:25:22.860 --> 00:25:25.900
from the point of view of law,

00:25:28.220 --> 00:25:29.380
there is no possibility

00:25:29.380 --> 00:25:33.560
to upset,

00:25:34.620 --> 00:25:35.920
to overthrow

00:25:35.920 --> 00:25:38.540
the decision of the Shukran Aruch.

00:25:39.400 --> 00:25:41.320
The only possibility would be

00:25:41.320 --> 00:25:43.820
that which was proposed

00:25:43.820 --> 00:25:45.960
by the first two

00:25:45.960 --> 00:25:48.500
chief rabbis of modern Israel.

00:25:49.840 --> 00:25:52.540
The Sephardic and the Ashkenazic rabbi.

00:25:53.140 --> 00:25:55.540
And if you allow me a little bit of

00:25:55.540 --> 00:25:56.620
personal comments,

00:25:56.940 --> 00:25:57.480
in my opinion,

00:25:57.480 --> 00:26:00.640
unmatched by any subsequent rabbis.

00:26:01.460 --> 00:26:03.180
And there was Isaac Herzog.

00:26:04.580 --> 00:26:06.440
You are familiar probably with his son,

00:26:06.500 --> 00:26:08.160
who is the president of Israel, Chaim Herzog.

00:26:09.560 --> 00:26:11.820
And Rav Uziel.

00:26:12.960 --> 00:26:15.940
And both of them believed that it was high time

00:26:15.940 --> 00:26:19.820
for the Jewish people to have to reconvene

00:26:21.040 --> 00:26:22.460
a Bedin of Musmachim

00:26:22.460 --> 00:26:25.600
with the same spirit as Yaakov B'Rav

00:26:25.600 --> 00:26:33.080
that will be able to revise and legally decide what Jewish law is all about.

00:26:33.080 --> 00:26:40.900
But until this project is done, the Shulchan Aruch remains a legal code.

00:26:41.960 --> 00:26:47.440
Now there are some ideas about these codes which are absolutely revolutionary.

00:26:47.440 --> 00:27:04.460
Number one, the need for unity. But the unity should be not one authority imposing itself on the rest of the Jewish community,

00:27:04.460 --> 00:27:07.380
but as he envisioned

00:27:07.380 --> 00:27:09.380
the three major Jewish communities

00:27:09.380 --> 00:27:11.980
compromising

00:27:11.980 --> 00:27:14.520
because this is what the Shulchan Aruch is

00:27:14.520 --> 00:27:16.080
compromising

00:27:16.080 --> 00:27:19.180
for the sake of uniformity

00:27:19.180 --> 00:27:20.700
in other words

00:27:20.700 --> 00:27:24.180
sometimes we will have to give up

00:27:24.180 --> 00:27:26.080
our own minhagim

00:27:26.080 --> 00:27:29.740
our own idiosyncrasies

00:27:29.740 --> 00:27:33.200
because the other segment of the Jewish community

00:27:33.200 --> 00:27:35.620
disagree with us.

00:27:38.360 --> 00:27:39.120
Compromise,

00:27:39.660 --> 00:27:41.600
according to Joseph Caro,

00:27:42.460 --> 00:27:44.840
it becomes an essential element

00:27:44.840 --> 00:27:47.120
in law.

00:27:47.700 --> 00:27:50.560
Rather than to have a geometrical view of law,

00:27:50.560 --> 00:27:54.180
that it is either my view or nothing,

00:27:55.260 --> 00:27:56.740
the Jewish communities

00:27:56.740 --> 00:27:58.200
have to learn

00:27:58.200 --> 00:28:01.560
how to negotiate and compromise.

00:28:01.560 --> 00:28:08.300
compromise, and ultimately from the point of view of God and the Hebrew tradition, it's

00:28:08.300 --> 00:28:16.080
not so important whether your view of the law is accepted, but rather the fact that

00:28:16.080 --> 00:28:24.140
all Jewish people are united in one idea. Compromise becomes one of the most important

00:28:24.140 --> 00:28:39.580
element of his law. Second, which is again, Jewish law has to be negotiated. And one of

00:28:39.580 --> 00:28:44.680
the things that he establishes in the Shulchan Aruch, in the introduction to the Bet Yosef,

00:28:44.680 --> 00:29:04.860
It's like this. A community has mit hakim, has customs, and those customs are to be respected up to the point that they will conflict with the welfare of the rest of the Jewish communities.

00:29:04.860 --> 00:29:13.040
In other words, rather than just insulate ourselves and think that only we are the ones who count,

00:29:13.700 --> 00:29:21.620
we must change and try to see the legal perspective from a total national view.

00:29:22.600 --> 00:29:26.560
What were the implications of the Shukran Ruch? What happened with the Shukran Ruch? And what did it do?

00:29:27.640 --> 00:29:30.880
First of all, it resulted into an economic boom.

00:29:30.880 --> 00:29:32.600
this is true

00:29:32.600 --> 00:29:35.620
the Shulchan Aruch was one of the great

00:29:35.620 --> 00:29:38.040
economic tools of the Jewish people

00:29:38.040 --> 00:29:40.000
and I explain you why

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:42.020
before

00:29:42.020 --> 00:29:43.060
the Shulchan Aruch

00:29:43.060 --> 00:29:46.000
international

00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:46.780
commerce

00:29:46.780 --> 00:29:49.560
whether you are Jewish or non-Jewish

00:29:49.560 --> 00:29:50.900
was impossible

00:29:50.900 --> 00:29:52.280
why?

00:29:53.180 --> 00:29:55.160
because if you have a merchandise

00:29:55.160 --> 00:29:57.000
that you are exporting

00:29:57.000 --> 00:29:59.960
to a different nation

00:29:59.960 --> 00:30:03.380
and then some conflicts will arise

00:30:03.380 --> 00:30:06.960
there was no tribunal on earth

00:30:06.960 --> 00:30:08.860
that could adjudicate

00:30:08.860 --> 00:30:11.620
between two autonomous nations

00:30:11.620 --> 00:30:14.100
let me give you a simple example

00:30:14.100 --> 00:30:16.260
out of literally thousands

00:30:16.260 --> 00:30:19.360
a boat

00:30:19.360 --> 00:30:22.680
belonging to a Jewish

00:30:22.680 --> 00:30:25.560
group in Venice

00:30:25.560 --> 00:30:29.620
was insured

00:30:29.620 --> 00:30:36.620
maritime insurance, a very important Jewish business. It was insured by a Saloniki family.

00:30:36.620 --> 00:30:45.620
A Jewish family in Saloniki, modern Greece, part of the Ottoman Empire at the time, insured

00:30:45.620 --> 00:30:58.620
the boat. The boat was in The Hague, Netherlands. While in the harbor there is a fire breaking

00:30:58.620 --> 00:31:03.540
breaking from the harbor, and reaching from the harbor, it reaches the boat.

00:31:04.760 --> 00:31:08.680
The boat is lost, while the boat was at the harbor.

00:31:10.420 --> 00:31:15.460
Now, the owners of the ship, of the boat, they claim they wanted the insurance.

00:31:18.240 --> 00:31:24.660
The insurance family, they say, well, the fire came not from the boat, but from the harbor.

00:31:25.480 --> 00:31:26.700
Yes? All right?

00:31:26.700 --> 00:31:30.240
Now, it involved three different countries.

00:31:30.980 --> 00:31:38.080
The Ottoman Empire, Saloniki, Venice, and the Netherlands.

00:31:39.060 --> 00:31:45.060
There was no tribunal on earth that could adjudicate this matter.

00:31:45.760 --> 00:31:51.140
Because we had the Shulchan Aruch, and because we had a code of law

00:31:51.140 --> 00:31:55.060
that was respected by every single Jewish community

00:31:55.060 --> 00:31:57.360
throughout the globe,

00:31:58.380 --> 00:32:01.560
all kinds of business transactions

00:32:01.560 --> 00:32:05.200
were in point of fact executed.

00:32:06.740 --> 00:32:07.900
The Shukran Aruch became

00:32:07.900 --> 00:32:11.960
the first international code of commerce.

00:32:13.540 --> 00:32:15.160
Because of this,

00:32:16.280 --> 00:32:18.560
Jewish scholarship flourished.

00:32:19.400 --> 00:32:19.800
Why?

00:32:21.140 --> 00:32:25.320
There is an aspect that no historian was able to unravel.

00:32:26.840 --> 00:32:35.040
And this was that the great supporters of the Jewish scholarship at the Ottoman Empire

00:32:35.040 --> 00:32:39.140
and throughout the Sephardic world were businessmen.

00:32:40.280 --> 00:32:46.080
Now, why businessmen were so much interested in sponsoring Jewish scholarship?

00:32:47.260 --> 00:32:48.580
It was business.

00:32:48.580 --> 00:32:50.480
and the reason is

00:32:50.480 --> 00:32:52.740
because through Jewish scholarship

00:32:52.740 --> 00:32:55.080
international

00:32:55.080 --> 00:32:57.220
law among Jews

00:32:57.220 --> 00:32:58.420
was possible

00:32:58.420 --> 00:33:01.140
the Jewish school

00:33:01.140 --> 00:33:03.400
became a school

00:33:03.400 --> 00:33:04.360
to train

00:33:04.360 --> 00:33:06.420
the future lawyers

00:33:06.420 --> 00:33:08.600
contracts

00:33:08.600 --> 00:33:10.540
were written by these individuals

00:33:10.540 --> 00:33:12.860
cases were defended, we have literally

00:33:12.860 --> 00:33:15.100
thousands and thousands of cases

00:33:15.100 --> 00:33:17.180
coming out from the Jewish

00:33:17.180 --> 00:33:17.740
schools

00:33:17.740 --> 00:33:20.420
the Jewish schools produce

00:33:20.420 --> 00:33:22.040
the future lawyers

00:33:22.040 --> 00:33:23.620
that will make

00:33:23.620 --> 00:33:26.380
international commerce possible

00:33:26.380 --> 00:33:27.720
so

00:33:27.720 --> 00:33:29.580
the Shulchan Aruch was able

00:33:29.580 --> 00:33:31.860
in a sense to enroll

00:33:31.860 --> 00:33:34.300
the business

00:33:34.300 --> 00:33:35.060
community

00:33:35.060 --> 00:33:37.040
behind it

00:33:37.040 --> 00:33:39.400
there was another thing

00:33:39.400 --> 00:33:42.220
revolutionized through the Shulchan Aruch

00:33:42.220 --> 00:33:44.440
since it became

00:33:44.440 --> 00:33:46.580
a code of pragmatic

00:33:46.580 --> 00:33:47.540
importance

00:33:47.540 --> 00:33:50.560
namely, you could do business

00:33:50.560 --> 00:33:51.660
through this code

00:33:51.660 --> 00:33:54.620
this code was not only

00:33:54.620 --> 00:33:56.860
respected throughout the whole entire world

00:33:56.860 --> 00:33:58.680
Sephardim and Ashkenazim

00:33:58.680 --> 00:34:00.460
but in a sense

00:34:00.460 --> 00:34:02.780
became the basis by which all the Jewish

00:34:02.780 --> 00:34:04.740
communities became united

00:34:04.740 --> 00:34:06.760
and there

00:34:06.760 --> 00:34:08.620
never was so much exchange

00:34:08.620 --> 00:34:11.020
both in populations

00:34:11.020 --> 00:34:12.460
and ideas

00:34:12.460 --> 00:34:14.880
between Sephardim and Ashkenazim

00:34:14.880 --> 00:34:16.720
as through the

00:34:16.720 --> 00:34:27.120
The Shukran Aruch became the basis of all possible relationship between different communities.

00:34:28.200 --> 00:34:42.140
Last but not least, traditionally, Talmudic studies were projected into the notion of dialectics.

00:34:42.140 --> 00:34:54.600
You have the pilpul. Pilpul are fine, sophisticated analysis of words, terms in the Talmud.

00:34:55.980 --> 00:35:04.040
What Joseph Caro made very clear is that this kind of analysis is a sterile.

00:35:04.040 --> 00:35:15.560
that the Talmud is basically a book that ought to be translated into legal terminology, into legal ideas.

00:35:16.160 --> 00:35:23.840
The power of the Shulchan Aruch is that the Talmud is a kind of a raw material.

00:35:24.480 --> 00:35:31.900
And unless we know how to formulate it into legal categories,

00:35:31.900 --> 00:35:37.760
it is not a useful type of enterprise

00:35:37.760 --> 00:35:44.520
once in this auditorium

00:35:44.520 --> 00:35:46.360
a few months ago

00:35:46.360 --> 00:35:49.660
I mentioned a story

00:35:49.660 --> 00:35:52.620
written by Joseph Caro himself

00:35:52.620 --> 00:35:55.280
and at the autobiographical note

00:35:55.280 --> 00:35:57.540
about himself

00:35:57.540 --> 00:36:03.140
in which he has a vision of an angel

00:36:03.140 --> 00:36:05.840
that comes and teaches him Torah.

00:36:08.300 --> 00:36:10.660
And there is a kind of discussion with this angel.

00:36:12.120 --> 00:36:18.000
Now, Joseph Caro was a very serious student of the Mishnah,

00:36:18.720 --> 00:36:21.640
the first Jewish legal code in history,

00:36:22.220 --> 00:36:23.540
written by Rabbeinu HaKadosh.

00:36:23.540 --> 00:36:26.300
there was a passage

00:36:26.300 --> 00:36:28.340
in that book

00:36:28.340 --> 00:36:31.400
that he was unable to unravel

00:36:31.400 --> 00:36:33.580
very difficult passage

00:36:33.580 --> 00:36:35.300
as a matter of fact

00:36:35.300 --> 00:36:36.860
he asked consults with all

00:36:36.860 --> 00:36:39.220
his colleagues

00:36:39.220 --> 00:36:40.820
nobody

00:36:40.820 --> 00:36:42.780
is able to explain

00:36:42.780 --> 00:36:43.980
the meaning of that passage

00:36:43.980 --> 00:36:47.120
he asked the angel

00:36:47.120 --> 00:36:50.900
he says what this passage means

00:36:50.900 --> 00:36:52.300
and the angel says

00:36:52.300 --> 00:37:01.380
oh, nobody was able to understand this passage, since it was given at Sinai.

00:37:02.260 --> 00:37:05.820
And I'm going to reveal the meaning of that passage to you and you alone.

00:37:06.780 --> 00:37:09.720
You're going to be the first one who knows the meaning of this passage.

00:37:10.940 --> 00:37:13.740
He gives them the meaning of the passage, explains to them the passage of the Mishnah,

00:37:14.600 --> 00:37:20.440
and Joseph Caro is so excited that he wants to go to the Red Medrash, to the school,

00:37:20.440 --> 00:37:22.480
and share it with his colleagues.

00:37:23.820 --> 00:37:25.920
As he's entering into the Pet Medrash,

00:37:27.360 --> 00:37:28.260
he sees a little boy,

00:37:29.240 --> 00:37:30.220
eight, nine years old,

00:37:31.100 --> 00:37:31.920
studying Mishnayot.

00:37:33.140 --> 00:37:34.420
And he happened to be studying

00:37:34.420 --> 00:37:35.580
that particular passage.

00:37:37.660 --> 00:37:39.760
So, Joseph Caro says,

00:37:40.140 --> 00:37:40.980
as to this child,

00:37:41.380 --> 00:37:42.600
what does it mean?

00:37:44.440 --> 00:37:45.220
And lo and behold,

00:37:45.560 --> 00:37:46.220
this child

00:37:46.220 --> 00:37:49.220
knows exactly what it means.

00:37:50.440 --> 00:37:57.540
Now he's puzzled, because the angel had told him that nobody knew it except for him.

00:37:59.540 --> 00:38:08.960
So he goes back to his house, prays, the angel comes, and says, there's something wrong with your claims.

00:38:09.880 --> 00:38:15.540
You told me that I'm the first one to know this passage, and I discovered there's a little boy, he knows it.

00:38:16.440 --> 00:38:18.120
He says, no, you were the first one.

00:38:18.120 --> 00:38:20.800
but after you brought this knowledge

00:38:20.800 --> 00:38:22.160
from heaven down to earth

00:38:22.160 --> 00:38:24.980
it becomes accessible to everyone

00:38:24.980 --> 00:38:28.820
one of the great things that Joseph Caro

00:38:28.820 --> 00:38:29.300
made

00:38:29.300 --> 00:38:33.180
was to bring down

00:38:33.180 --> 00:38:34.940
Jewish law

00:38:34.940 --> 00:38:36.980
from the

00:38:36.980 --> 00:38:39.160
intricacies and the labyrinths

00:38:39.160 --> 00:38:41.680
of

00:38:41.680 --> 00:38:44.180
populistic discussions

00:38:44.180 --> 00:38:46.660
into a shulchan aruch

00:38:46.660 --> 00:38:50.700
Shukran al-Rukh means a well-prepared table.

00:38:51.800 --> 00:38:52.900
Everything is ready.

00:38:54.100 --> 00:38:55.900
It is up to you to stretch your hand,

00:38:56.920 --> 00:38:58.000
to take it,

00:38:58.760 --> 00:38:59.900
and to take advantage of it.

00:39:01.260 --> 00:39:05.640
In a sense, Shukran al-Rukh meant the liberation,

00:39:06.940 --> 00:39:09.000
freedom of the Jew

00:39:09.000 --> 00:39:13.820
from the pitfalls of the clergy.

00:39:13.820 --> 00:39:17.600
before the Shulchan Aruch

00:39:17.600 --> 00:39:21.760
Jewish law was the exclusive privilege of a clergy

00:39:21.760 --> 00:39:27.440
a clergy that the common lay person was unable to challenge

00:39:27.440 --> 00:39:31.180
law could be so complex

00:39:31.180 --> 00:39:35.060
that an individual could be arbitrary

00:39:35.060 --> 00:39:37.420
decide in one way one day

00:39:37.420 --> 00:39:39.820
in the other way the other

00:39:39.820 --> 00:39:41.720
there was a grip

00:39:41.720 --> 00:39:48.200
that the clergy had Jewish clergy over the Jewish people.

00:39:49.400 --> 00:39:59.940
We do know that one of the crucial reasons why some Jews prefer conversion to Judaism

00:39:59.940 --> 00:40:08.680
because many Jews felt that the oppression of the clergy was unbearable.

00:40:08.680 --> 00:40:11.500
in a sense

00:40:11.500 --> 00:40:13.560
in a sense

00:40:13.560 --> 00:40:15.680
by

00:40:15.680 --> 00:40:17.400
formulating

00:40:17.400 --> 00:40:19.380
Jewish law

00:40:19.380 --> 00:40:22.160
in a simple way

00:40:22.160 --> 00:40:24.160
and by

00:40:24.160 --> 00:40:26.220
formulating Jewish law in a way that is

00:40:26.220 --> 00:40:27.180
not only simple

00:40:27.180 --> 00:40:30.140
but is legally

00:40:30.140 --> 00:40:31.880
meaningful

00:40:31.880 --> 00:40:32.840
binding

00:40:32.840 --> 00:40:36.200
the Shulchan Aruch became

00:40:36.200 --> 00:40:36.920
the book

00:40:36.920 --> 00:40:40.020
by which the lay person

00:40:40.020 --> 00:40:43.260
could declare his independence

00:40:43.260 --> 00:40:45.740
from the clergy.

00:40:46.800 --> 00:40:49.080
Let me summarize.

00:40:52.020 --> 00:40:54.080
The Shulchan Aruch is the dream

00:40:54.080 --> 00:40:56.620
of a little boy

00:40:56.620 --> 00:40:58.780
leaving Toledo

00:40:58.780 --> 00:41:01.900
and seeing the world,

00:41:01.900 --> 00:41:03.160
the Jewish world,

00:41:03.540 --> 00:41:04.800
coming into ashes.

00:41:06.920 --> 00:41:09.180
Toledo was a cosmopolitan city.

00:41:10.600 --> 00:41:11.880
Different cultures together.

00:41:13.560 --> 00:41:17.220
Arabic-speaking Jews, Jews from France, Jews from Germany,

00:41:18.280 --> 00:41:20.320
Spanish-speaking, they're all together.

00:41:22.460 --> 00:41:24.500
It was turned into ashes.

00:41:26.260 --> 00:41:29.540
As this boy goes through the Ottoman Empire,

00:41:29.540 --> 00:41:33.480
he registers

00:41:33.480 --> 00:41:35.420
the bitter

00:41:35.420 --> 00:41:36.900
divisions

00:41:36.900 --> 00:41:40.160
plaguing the Jewish world

00:41:40.160 --> 00:41:44.300
he says in the time of Bechamai and Betilel

00:41:44.300 --> 00:41:46.520
there were two Torahs

00:41:46.520 --> 00:41:48.500
and the rabbis complain

00:41:48.500 --> 00:41:52.500
in our days we have numberless

00:41:52.500 --> 00:41:54.380
Torahs

00:41:54.380 --> 00:41:55.820
everybody

00:41:55.820 --> 00:42:05.000
wants to expose his views and declare all other Jews second rate.

00:42:06.800 --> 00:42:12.020
There was no respect for authority because the Jew did not respect his own self.

00:42:13.820 --> 00:42:14.860
What to do?

00:42:16.780 --> 00:42:19.940
In a sense, he created a new concept of authority.

00:42:19.940 --> 00:42:22.940
if we cannot be

00:42:22.940 --> 00:42:24.300
physically

00:42:24.300 --> 00:42:26.820
geographically

00:42:26.820 --> 00:42:28.340
politically together

00:42:28.340 --> 00:42:30.980
at least we could gather

00:42:30.980 --> 00:42:32.880
the Jewish minds of the past

00:42:32.880 --> 00:42:35.620
and all of us

00:42:35.620 --> 00:42:39.440
through the respect to our past

00:42:39.440 --> 00:42:42.340
find unity

00:42:42.340 --> 00:42:45.040
and authority for our present

00:42:45.040 --> 00:42:48.160
I always saw

00:42:48.160 --> 00:42:50.720
what happened to the Jew in Spain

00:42:50.720 --> 00:42:54.840
as a parallel to what happened to the Jews

00:42:54.840 --> 00:42:56.460
in modern times with the Holocaust.

00:42:58.140 --> 00:43:00.260
In both situations,

00:43:00.720 --> 00:43:02.680
we saw our dreams

00:43:02.680 --> 00:43:05.560
turn into ashes.

00:43:07.020 --> 00:43:09.200
In both situations,

00:43:10.640 --> 00:43:13.600
the Jew was bitter against himself

00:43:13.600 --> 00:43:14.680
and against another Jew.

00:43:14.680 --> 00:43:18.920
in both situations there was a need

00:43:18.920 --> 00:43:20.460
for authority

00:43:20.460 --> 00:43:22.640
Joseph Caro

00:43:22.640 --> 00:43:25.540
and his generation founded the Shuhana Ruch

00:43:25.540 --> 00:43:29.500
our generation founded the state of Israel

00:43:29.500 --> 00:43:32.100
in both cases

00:43:32.100 --> 00:43:33.880
we are searching

00:43:33.880 --> 00:43:37.420
for the rebirth of Jewish authority

00:43:37.420 --> 00:43:39.740
in both cases

00:43:39.740 --> 00:43:41.500
we look into the past

00:43:41.500 --> 00:43:43.800
and it is the lay person

00:43:43.800 --> 00:43:46.340
the layman, the laywoman

00:43:46.340 --> 00:43:48.340
that by

00:43:48.340 --> 00:43:50.600
consenting in that authority

00:43:50.600 --> 00:43:52.420
is given it

00:43:52.420 --> 00:43:54.040
its semicha

00:43:54.040 --> 00:43:56.180
the parallel thing

00:43:56.180 --> 00:43:58.200
is very important and is very deep

00:43:58.200 --> 00:44:00.120
thank you very much for your attention

00:44:13.800 --> 00:44:19.980
I'd like to thank Dr. Fowler for this marvelous presentation.

00:44:21.180 --> 00:44:29.780
The two things that are always amazing are he never uses notes.

00:44:30.880 --> 00:44:32.040
There were no notes up here.

00:44:33.540 --> 00:44:36.620
And the second thing is that when he came in this morning, he said to me,

00:44:36.660 --> 00:44:37.680
how long should I speak?

00:44:37.720 --> 00:44:39.080
And I said, about 45 minutes.

00:44:39.120 --> 00:44:41.500
If you look at your watch, it's exactly 45 minutes.

00:44:41.500 --> 00:44:44.960
so I wonder how many of you could do that

00:44:44.960 --> 00:44:49.260
now while he's catching his breath

00:44:49.260 --> 00:44:50.840
before the question and answer period

00:44:50.840 --> 00:44:52.120
a number of announcements

00:44:52.120 --> 00:44:55.240
first of all we have prepared a reading list

00:44:55.240 --> 00:44:57.640
for you, you can get them at the door if you haven't already

00:44:57.640 --> 00:45:00.520
of works from our Asher Library

00:45:00.520 --> 00:45:02.600
by Professor Faor

00:45:02.600 --> 00:45:05.480
as well as works on Joseph Caro

00:45:05.480 --> 00:45:06.960
secondly

00:45:06.960 --> 00:45:09.680
I would like to announce the dates

00:45:09.680 --> 00:45:11.420
of the three next Goldman Lectures

00:45:11.420 --> 00:45:14.640
and if you're not on our mailing list for the Goldman Lectures,

00:45:14.800 --> 00:45:18.660
please speak to our staff outside after the program today.

00:45:19.320 --> 00:45:24.240
The next lecture will be on December 4th, Sunday, December 4th,

00:45:24.240 --> 00:45:28.780
when we will be celebrating another birthday commemoration,

00:45:29.380 --> 00:45:35.820
the 700th anniversary of the birth of Rabbi Levi Ben Gershon Gersonides.

00:45:35.820 --> 00:45:41.720
and the speaker at that time will be Professor Norbert Samuelson of Temple University,

00:45:41.920 --> 00:45:43.920
who, by the way, is a native Chicagoan.

00:45:44.600 --> 00:45:52.820
The lecture after that, February 12th, will be by our visiting professor here at Spurters College for Winter 1989.

00:45:53.560 --> 00:45:58.880
Many of you know him, Professor Leonard Fine, founder of Moment Magazine,

00:45:59.320 --> 00:46:04.960
and he will be speaking on Herzl's books, The Jewish State and the Old New Land,

00:46:04.960 --> 00:46:08.100
and their relationship to the state of Israel today.

00:46:08.920 --> 00:46:14.000
And on March 12th, exactly a month later,

00:46:14.520 --> 00:46:16.520
our visiting professor for the spring quarter,

00:46:16.680 --> 00:46:19.900
who many of you have heard a few weeks ago, Professor Howard Schwartz,

00:46:20.740 --> 00:46:24.620
will be speaking about the tales of Rabbi Nachman of Bratislava.

00:46:28.800 --> 00:46:34.640
Our very exciting courses given by our very fine faculty,

00:46:34.960 --> 00:46:39.820
including Professor Faor, Professor Fine, myself and others.

00:46:40.640 --> 00:46:44.100
And also outside the door, if you don't believe we have a very fine faculty,

00:46:44.460 --> 00:46:50.060
you'll find a copy of the October 11th U.S. News and World Report,

00:46:50.360 --> 00:46:54.600
which rated the Spurdis College faculty one of the top 20 in the United States.

00:47:00.720 --> 00:47:03.540
Now Professor Faor will be happy to entertain questions.

00:47:03.540 --> 00:47:06.380
if you have a question please just step to the microphone

00:47:06.380 --> 00:47:07.260
in the middle of the room

00:47:07.260 --> 00:47:11.340
we have been taught

00:47:11.340 --> 00:47:13.360
a famous expression

00:47:13.360 --> 00:47:17.500
the law of the land prevails

00:47:17.500 --> 00:47:19.020
those who live outside Israel

00:47:19.020 --> 00:47:21.920
must abide by the law of the land

00:47:21.920 --> 00:47:22.640
in which they live

00:47:22.640 --> 00:47:24.520
under what conditions

00:47:24.520 --> 00:47:27.500
are we permitted not to abide by the law of the land

00:47:27.500 --> 00:47:29.820
under what conditions may we be allowed

00:47:29.820 --> 00:47:31.000
not to

00:47:31.000 --> 00:47:33.160
observe strictly what

00:47:33.160 --> 00:47:35.480
that Shulchan Aruch dictates?

00:47:36.840 --> 00:47:39.060
First of all, a very important notion.

00:47:39.440 --> 00:47:44.560
The Jew, before Napoleon,

00:47:45.320 --> 00:47:47.320
considered himself as a nation,

00:47:47.440 --> 00:47:50.560
as an autonomous nation in exile.

00:47:51.400 --> 00:47:53.540
As a matter of fact, when Napoleon offered citizenship

00:47:53.540 --> 00:47:55.980
to the Sephardic Jews in Amsterdam,

00:47:57.100 --> 00:48:00.740
the Sephardic Jews refused to accept citizenship

00:48:00.740 --> 00:48:05.680
because citizenship will mean, therefore, that you have to abide by the law,

00:48:05.800 --> 00:48:08.620
you have to dismantle your Jewish courts,

00:48:09.120 --> 00:48:12.520
and in point of fact, and this is a very interesting, delicate issue,

00:48:13.160 --> 00:48:16.240
renounce to the land of Israel because if you're a citizen of a country,

00:48:16.860 --> 00:48:19.780
you're going to say, I'm in Golos and I want to have another country.

00:48:20.600 --> 00:48:25.480
So for a while, the whole notion of citizenship and so on,

00:48:25.480 --> 00:48:28.200
it was a very, very important issue.

00:48:28.200 --> 00:48:38.540
But to be brief and direct to your question, at the time of the Shulchan Aruch, the Jews conceived themselves as a nation in exile.

00:48:39.020 --> 00:48:49.020
So much so that when the first Jews arrived to America, and they had this, you know, with the governor of New Amsterdam, Stuyvesant,

00:48:49.460 --> 00:48:52.460
one of the reasons why they were not so much welcome in America,

00:48:52.460 --> 00:49:00.260
because explicitly they said that we should be recognized as members of the Jewish nation in exile.

00:49:01.040 --> 00:49:04.420
Therefore, for they didn't serve in the army, they didn't pay taxes individually.

00:49:05.080 --> 00:49:06.980
They paid taxes only as a body.

00:49:06.980 --> 00:49:07.580
All right.

00:49:07.740 --> 00:49:10.000
That is so far as history is concerned.

00:49:10.840 --> 00:49:17.760
From the point of view of Judaism today, we do observe all the laws of the Malchuta

00:49:17.760 --> 00:49:26.480
as long as they don't interfere with either family law or ritual.

00:49:27.420 --> 00:49:31.820
And thank God that we happen to be living in America

00:49:31.820 --> 00:49:34.880
in which there is separation of church and state,

00:49:35.380 --> 00:49:40.060
and here we could be a full American citizen and a full Jew.

00:49:40.060 --> 00:49:43.240
So in this country we have absolutely no problem

00:49:43.240 --> 00:49:46.500
because there is a separation of church and state.

00:49:46.500 --> 00:49:59.960
And the Jewish law says very clearly, you obey all the laws of the state as long as they don't interfere with the basic Jewish law.

00:50:00.140 --> 00:50:02.080
Let me give you an example, a very important example.

00:50:03.680 --> 00:50:10.780
According to Protestant ethics, let's see Luther.

00:50:10.780 --> 00:50:15.420
an individual has to obey the state

00:50:15.420 --> 00:50:18.780
even though the state will tell him to do something against his conscience

00:50:18.780 --> 00:50:20.960
which therefore means

00:50:20.960 --> 00:50:23.660
that somebody like Eichmann

00:50:23.660 --> 00:50:27.500
according to that system of thinking

00:50:27.500 --> 00:50:31.720
is excused because he has to follow what the state tells him

00:50:31.720 --> 00:50:33.100
according to Judaism

00:50:33.100 --> 00:50:35.540
we obey the state up to a point

00:50:35.540 --> 00:50:37.120
that the state will tell us

00:50:37.120 --> 00:50:38.500
if the state would tell me

00:50:38.500 --> 00:50:40.540
go and work in a concentration camp

00:50:40.540 --> 00:50:46.180
and from 9 to 5 and kill little children, men, women, and this, we say no to the state.

00:50:46.280 --> 00:50:47.500
That is part of Jewish tradition.

00:50:48.560 --> 00:50:53.500
So therefore Jewish tradition is very careful to distinguish between those laws

00:50:53.500 --> 00:50:58.680
that do not contravene basic scriptural commitment

00:50:58.680 --> 00:51:04.580
and other, the commercial, financial laws of the state that we have to obey in full.

00:51:04.580 --> 00:51:10.780
Professor Faur, you indicated that

00:51:10.780 --> 00:51:14.560
Joseph Caro made a shulchan aruch

00:51:14.560 --> 00:51:17.140
that would apply to the entire Jewish people

00:51:17.140 --> 00:51:21.160
would you comment on the Mappa of Isilas?

00:51:21.460 --> 00:51:23.520
Yes, very important question that you're raising

00:51:23.520 --> 00:51:26.020
and that's one of the reasons I did want to elaborate

00:51:26.020 --> 00:51:30.080
because I knew that the question is going to be brought into the subject

00:51:30.080 --> 00:51:33.140
there is of course

00:51:33.140 --> 00:51:34.980
the famous Rabbi Moshe

00:51:34.980 --> 00:51:37.020
Isselin from

00:51:37.020 --> 00:51:38.680
Poland, Krakow,

00:51:39.260 --> 00:51:40.700
who wrote

00:51:40.700 --> 00:51:42.020
notes

00:51:42.020 --> 00:51:44.980
in which many, many points

00:51:44.980 --> 00:51:47.080
disagrees with Joseph Karo.

00:51:48.000 --> 00:51:49.200
Two very

00:51:49.200 --> 00:51:50.220
important observations.

00:51:51.000 --> 00:51:53.280
Number one, there was a very lively

00:51:53.280 --> 00:51:55.440
and friendly correspondence

00:51:55.440 --> 00:51:57.320
between both

00:51:57.320 --> 00:51:59.040
Joseph Karo and

00:51:59.040 --> 00:51:59.620
Rabbi Moshe.

00:52:00.480 --> 00:52:02.080
We have the two votes.

00:52:02.080 --> 00:52:05.020
beautiful, very nice comradeship

00:52:05.020 --> 00:52:05.880
and respect

00:52:05.880 --> 00:52:07.420
second

00:52:07.420 --> 00:52:10.460
the very fact

00:52:10.460 --> 00:52:12.340
not only the Ramah

00:52:12.340 --> 00:52:14.980
but the countless

00:52:14.980 --> 00:52:16.960
Ashkenazi commentaries

00:52:16.960 --> 00:52:19.020
write notes

00:52:19.020 --> 00:52:20.720
or notes rather

00:52:20.720 --> 00:52:21.580
to the Shulchan Aruch

00:52:21.580 --> 00:52:24.680
only strengthen the Shulchan Aruch

00:52:24.680 --> 00:52:27.000
all what the Ramah says

00:52:27.000 --> 00:52:29.020
says that in our

00:52:29.020 --> 00:52:29.700
particular

00:52:29.700 --> 00:52:32.080
city or place,

00:52:32.720 --> 00:52:34.100
we have a different custom.

00:52:34.820 --> 00:52:36.700
In other words, this is the law.

00:52:37.140 --> 00:52:38.320
Shukran Aruch is the law.

00:52:38.780 --> 00:52:40.060
We have different customs.

00:52:40.060 --> 00:52:41.820
And he points the custom

00:52:41.820 --> 00:52:44.260
and in a way makes it easier

00:52:44.260 --> 00:52:46.080
for the Shukran Aruch

00:52:46.080 --> 00:52:48.100
to acclimatize itself

00:52:48.100 --> 00:52:49.860
to

00:52:49.860 --> 00:52:52.240
Eastern European communities.

00:52:52.840 --> 00:52:54.120
If the Shukran Aruch

00:52:54.120 --> 00:52:55.800
would have remained without the Hama,

00:52:57.840 --> 00:52:58.560
it would have been

00:52:58.560 --> 00:52:59.360
rejected.

00:52:59.700 --> 00:53:07.040
because we know how people are, people don't like to abandon family or community tradition.

00:53:07.820 --> 00:53:17.600
By writing those glosses, the Raman makes it possible to accept the Shulchan Aruch in Eastern European communities.

00:53:17.600 --> 00:53:23.440
So I don't see it as anti-Shulchan Aruch, but rather I see it as pro-Shulchan Aruch.

00:53:24.500 --> 00:53:28.820
And one of the great countries, and that's the way Mappa, you know what the word Mappa means?

00:53:28.820 --> 00:53:30.520
a table cloth

00:53:30.520 --> 00:53:33.420
and he's just doing something

00:53:33.420 --> 00:53:34.660
adding to it

00:53:34.660 --> 00:53:36.780
he's making it fancier

00:53:36.780 --> 00:53:39.720
so it's not a negation of

00:53:39.720 --> 00:53:41.360
but a strengthen of

00:53:41.360 --> 00:53:42.220
the Shulchan Aruch

00:53:42.220 --> 00:53:48.800
I wish Dr. Fowler

00:53:48.800 --> 00:53:50.400
get to explain

00:53:50.400 --> 00:53:53.140
what the Shulchan Aruch say to such

00:53:53.140 --> 00:53:55.520
seems to me difficult

00:53:55.520 --> 00:53:57.460
I learn once

00:53:57.460 --> 00:53:58.020
in Geda

00:53:58.020 --> 00:54:01.120
in Numbers, in the Torah,

00:54:02.200 --> 00:54:03.080
the Midbar Jew,

00:54:04.000 --> 00:54:05.900
they got their sticks in Sabbath.

00:54:07.500 --> 00:54:09.200
There was the law of God.

00:54:11.200 --> 00:54:13.360
Other law in Deuteronomy,

00:54:13.600 --> 00:54:14.340
in Deuteronomy,

00:54:15.180 --> 00:54:17.560
is a law if a man gets married,

00:54:18.420 --> 00:54:19.140
in this guild,

00:54:19.140 --> 00:54:20.680
he knows his wife,

00:54:20.820 --> 00:54:23.520
next day they find out she was not a virgin,

00:54:24.200 --> 00:54:25.520
she will be stoned to death.

00:54:25.520 --> 00:54:27.660
in such a law

00:54:27.660 --> 00:54:29.300
but a rebellious son

00:54:29.300 --> 00:54:31.200
a son, a murderer

00:54:31.200 --> 00:54:33.100
not obey father and mother

00:54:33.100 --> 00:54:34.460
the same thing

00:54:34.460 --> 00:54:37.180
but I not contest the law

00:54:37.180 --> 00:54:39.620
that he should be stoned to death

00:54:39.620 --> 00:54:41.920
I'm not authority

00:54:41.920 --> 00:54:44.260
I'm a plain common Jew

00:54:44.260 --> 00:54:46.020
but I wonder

00:54:46.020 --> 00:54:47.720
why should not

00:54:47.720 --> 00:54:49.120
the authorities

00:54:49.120 --> 00:54:51.820
put a special

00:54:51.820 --> 00:54:52.300
argument

00:54:52.300 --> 00:54:55.120
he should kill, he should stone

00:54:55.120 --> 00:54:57.520
why should I put my hands in blood

00:54:57.520 --> 00:54:59.600
they say the Torah says

00:54:59.600 --> 00:55:02.040
kol b'nei

00:55:02.040 --> 00:55:02.540
Eidu

00:55:02.540 --> 00:55:05.240
on another place say

00:55:05.240 --> 00:55:06.340
kol b'nei Eidu

00:55:06.340 --> 00:55:09.260
all the citizens, the men from this guild

00:55:09.260 --> 00:55:11.500
in this state, in this village

00:55:11.500 --> 00:55:12.800
they shall stone

00:55:12.800 --> 00:55:14.260
why should I stone

00:55:14.260 --> 00:55:16.800
we are about to say the Shulchan Aruch to this

00:55:16.800 --> 00:55:19.880
that is one of the great contributions of the Shulchan Aruch

00:55:19.880 --> 00:55:20.680
is precisely

00:55:20.680 --> 00:55:23.300
in omitting anything to do

00:55:23.300 --> 00:55:24.620
with capital punishment

00:55:24.620 --> 00:55:26.980
and therefore because he says very clearly

00:55:26.980 --> 00:55:28.100
that capital punishment

00:55:28.100 --> 00:55:31.300
is no longer to be practiced

00:55:31.300 --> 00:55:32.320
among Jews

00:55:32.320 --> 00:55:34.960
so therefore all the problems involved

00:55:34.960 --> 00:55:36.940
with laws which by the time

00:55:36.940 --> 00:55:39.180
that the Shukran Aruch was composed

00:55:39.180 --> 00:55:41.180
were no longer part of the

00:55:41.180 --> 00:55:43.360
civilized horizon

00:55:43.360 --> 00:55:45.680
the Shukran Aruch very intelligently

00:55:45.680 --> 00:55:46.920
he

00:55:46.920 --> 00:55:49.360
solves the problem

00:55:49.360 --> 00:55:50.640
by saying

00:55:50.640 --> 00:55:52.740
capital cases

00:55:52.740 --> 00:55:54.380
no longer

00:55:54.380 --> 00:55:56.560
tried by Jews

00:55:56.560 --> 00:55:58.120
and by omitting

00:55:58.120 --> 00:56:01.120
and in a way

00:56:01.120 --> 00:56:03.000
the Shukah Aruch becomes stronger

00:56:03.000 --> 00:56:03.800
and stronger

00:56:03.800 --> 00:56:05.860
and this is the answer to your question

00:56:05.860 --> 00:56:08.620
all those laws are just

00:56:08.620 --> 00:56:10.220
omitted

00:56:10.220 --> 00:56:11.540
by the Shukah Aruch

00:56:11.540 --> 00:56:12.940
not brought into

00:56:12.940 --> 00:56:15.640
the Torah is a law

00:56:15.640 --> 00:56:17.520
every Jewish boy

00:56:17.520 --> 00:56:20.140
by 20 must serve in the army

00:56:20.140 --> 00:56:21.820
that is an exception

00:56:21.820 --> 00:56:24.980
if a man

00:56:24.980 --> 00:56:26.000
up not his heart

00:56:26.000 --> 00:56:28.700
he shall be relieved

00:56:28.700 --> 00:56:30.620
why I should not be relieved

00:56:30.620 --> 00:56:31.120
from this

00:56:31.120 --> 00:56:33.720
I'm just saying

00:56:33.720 --> 00:56:36.420
Joseph Caro has none of the laws

00:56:36.420 --> 00:56:37.500
applying to army

00:56:37.500 --> 00:56:40.460
to anything to do with the shedding

00:56:40.460 --> 00:56:41.160
of blood

00:56:41.160 --> 00:56:42.620
in any way

00:56:42.620 --> 00:56:46.000
they are eliminated by the

00:56:46.000 --> 00:56:48.080
it does not try them

00:56:48.080 --> 00:56:49.560
and that in a sense

00:56:49.560 --> 00:56:51.360
Jewish law becomes much stronger

00:56:51.360 --> 00:56:53.500
because of this. Yes, ma'am?

00:56:54.280 --> 00:56:56.200
This Ramah that you mentioned,

00:56:56.400 --> 00:56:57.920
is that the same thing

00:56:57.920 --> 00:56:58.860
as the Ramuh?

00:56:59.440 --> 00:56:59.960
Exactly.

00:57:01.180 --> 00:57:02.720
And when did he live?

00:57:03.060 --> 00:57:05.020
He lived at the same time. By the way,

00:57:05.340 --> 00:57:06.940
he died, interesting,

00:57:07.440 --> 00:57:10.000
he was a junior in age to Maran,

00:57:10.600 --> 00:57:11.440
but he lived,

00:57:11.440 --> 00:57:13.440
he did not make it to the 40 years.

00:57:13.600 --> 00:57:14.100
He lived about

00:57:14.100 --> 00:57:16.560
33 years old.

00:57:17.280 --> 00:57:19.420
And Maran lived 87 years old.

00:57:19.560 --> 00:57:24.820
So the Ramah were contemporaries.

00:57:25.400 --> 00:57:26.460
They wrote to each other.

00:57:27.060 --> 00:57:30.020
Beautiful, beautiful chivot, beautiful response.

00:57:32.240 --> 00:57:35.480
But Maran, Joseph Haro, outlived him.

00:57:36.360 --> 00:57:40.540
So the Ramah and the Ramoh is the same way, just a different differentiation.

00:57:41.400 --> 00:57:44.040
Is that the Rabbi Isabel?

00:57:45.080 --> 00:57:46.660
Not Isabel, Isabel.

00:57:47.480 --> 00:57:48.000
Moshe.

00:57:48.640 --> 00:57:49.000
Moshe.

00:57:49.000 --> 00:57:51.240
And where does this Ramah...

00:57:51.240 --> 00:57:51.660
Krakow.

00:57:52.560 --> 00:57:53.200
In Krakow.

00:57:53.800 --> 00:57:54.320
No, no, no.

00:57:54.860 --> 00:57:55.380
Initials?

00:57:56.200 --> 00:57:58.660
The Ramah means Rav, Moshe, Israel.

00:57:59.100 --> 00:57:59.500
Okay.

00:58:00.300 --> 00:58:00.660
Thank you.

00:58:00.820 --> 00:58:05.140
But they call him Ramah because Ramah in Hebrew sounds like high.

00:58:05.500 --> 00:58:06.520
You know, somebody high.

00:58:06.820 --> 00:58:07.120
Ram.

00:58:07.480 --> 00:58:07.660
You know.

00:58:07.940 --> 00:58:10.000
That's a nice, you know...

00:58:10.820 --> 00:58:12.600
Where did he live?

00:58:12.820 --> 00:58:13.420
In Krakow.

00:58:13.840 --> 00:58:14.320
Krakow.

00:58:14.560 --> 00:58:15.000
Thank you.

00:58:15.000 --> 00:58:20.140
I wonder if you can comment on the Magid.

00:58:21.160 --> 00:58:28.820
Was it a real Magid, a Schliach from heaven, or it was an auto-suggestion,

00:58:29.420 --> 00:58:32.120
or maybe it was just an echo of his thought?

00:58:32.860 --> 00:58:35.100
Well, this is a very difficult question to answer.

00:58:35.240 --> 00:58:38.640
I know there are some people, there is a book written on Joseph Karo,

00:58:38.720 --> 00:58:42.860
in which this subject is analyzed, and some people would say that,

00:58:42.860 --> 00:58:48.560
I mean, briefly, let me tell you, according to our cultural standard today,

00:58:49.460 --> 00:58:52.700
if somebody in our culture would say an angel is talking to me,

00:58:54.140 --> 00:58:58.720
he will be considered mildly schizophrenic.

00:58:59.700 --> 00:59:10.200
But as psychologists teach us, madness and sanity is conditioned by culture.

00:59:10.200 --> 00:59:18.520
And what in one culture could be considered as mad, in another culture is considered as totally normal.

00:59:18.520 --> 00:59:21.880
And not only in question of time, but also in space.

00:59:21.880 --> 00:59:34.360
For instance, would you consider some of the behavior, say, of people in India, Japan, China, Australian aborigines, American Indians?

00:59:34.360 --> 00:59:41.900
If you compare it to what we do, well, we would say that person maybe is not considered normal from our standard.

00:59:42.960 --> 00:59:50.380
But psychologists say that we have to be a little bit more relativistic and realize that sanity and normalness,

00:59:50.860 --> 00:59:57.900
whatever is normal, it is conditioned by time and society.

00:59:57.900 --> 01:00:05.820
So again, I would say, whether he was a saint or not, or this, I mean, I cannot answer.

01:00:05.960 --> 01:00:06.420
I'm not qualified.

01:00:06.540 --> 01:00:13.760
The only thing I could say, that in that time, in that society, visions with angels was considered normal.

01:00:14.000 --> 01:00:16.220
That's the only thing I could answer, but I cannot go more than that.

01:00:16.240 --> 01:00:21.120
Is there any traces in the Shulchan Aruch, any mystical traces?

01:00:21.120 --> 01:00:22.120
Very important question.

01:00:22.460 --> 01:00:25.560
This is a very, very, I appreciate the question, because really it is.

01:00:25.560 --> 01:00:32.000
One of the important elements, although the Shukran Aruch himself was a mystic and believed in mysticism,

01:00:32.580 --> 01:00:36.460
you find zero trace of mysticism in the Shukran Aruch.

01:00:36.920 --> 01:00:45.840
He really was able to control whatever mystical ideals he had and to leave it only in the realm of the very, very private.

01:00:46.620 --> 01:00:50.260
In point of fact, his book, Magid Mishalim, he did not publish.

01:00:50.660 --> 01:00:54.120
It was published after his death by his students.

01:00:54.600 --> 01:00:55.160
Yes?

01:00:55.160 --> 01:00:58.540
so for him the mysticism

01:00:58.540 --> 01:01:00.780
was a personal

01:01:00.780 --> 01:01:01.780
experience

01:01:01.780 --> 01:01:04.520
and he was not interested in sharing this

01:01:04.520 --> 01:01:06.200
with the rest of the world

01:01:06.200 --> 01:01:08.700
and the Shokharu

01:01:08.700 --> 01:01:10.160
have no traces of it, none

01:01:10.160 --> 01:01:16.020
two questions please

01:01:16.020 --> 01:01:18.760
first of all to what extent do you think Rabbi Karo

01:01:18.760 --> 01:01:20.640
expected his treatise to be considered

01:01:20.640 --> 01:01:21.740
normative for the future

01:01:21.740 --> 01:01:23.780
as opposed to just the period in which he left

01:01:24.440 --> 01:01:29.440
And secondly, to the extent that it was supported because of its economic, political, and social implications,

01:01:30.120 --> 01:01:33.420
do you see that as a possible model for resolving some of the issues in Israel today?

01:01:33.960 --> 01:01:37.800
Well, let me begin with an important observation.

01:01:37.800 --> 01:01:44.580
The decay of or the loss of authority of the Shulchan Aruch comes exactly at the time

01:01:44.580 --> 01:01:47.840
when Napoleon establishes his international law,

01:01:48.280 --> 01:01:51.200
and therefore the Jew, rather than to rely on the Shulchan Aruch,

01:01:51.200 --> 01:01:54.200
he realized international law to do his business.

01:01:54.860 --> 01:01:57.820
So here you see that there was a relationship, a very strong relationship,

01:01:57.820 --> 01:02:01.500
between pragmatics and Torah.

01:02:01.920 --> 01:02:03.220
You see it very clearly.

01:02:03.420 --> 01:02:10.380
As soon as the Jews had other courts besides the Jewish court,

01:02:10.460 --> 01:02:12.580
then they preferred, they took the business,

01:02:12.820 --> 01:02:17.160
and if you have a claim, you would use a regular, normal, private international law.

01:02:17.460 --> 01:02:18.420
That's what you apply.

01:02:18.420 --> 01:02:25.360
Now, what is important, I believe, of the Shulchan Aruch, the two things I think is important.

01:02:26.540 --> 01:02:35.260
Number one, that every generation or every couple of generations, they should have a code.

01:02:36.160 --> 01:02:41.380
And the law should not be left to the arbitrary whims of the clergy.

01:02:41.940 --> 01:02:43.740
This, I think, is terribly important.

01:02:43.740 --> 01:02:45.780
because otherwise

01:02:45.780 --> 01:02:48.640
there is a possibility of abuse

01:02:48.640 --> 01:02:50.340
or the appearance of abuse

01:02:50.340 --> 01:02:52.480
I think that today, even today

01:02:52.480 --> 01:02:54.440
where many Jews who are committed

01:02:54.440 --> 01:02:56.300
ideologically to

01:02:56.300 --> 01:02:58.540
Jewish law, they find it

01:02:58.540 --> 01:02:59.720
a little bit uncomfortable

01:02:59.720 --> 01:03:02.480
to submit to

01:03:02.480 --> 01:03:03.980
what appears the whims

01:03:03.980 --> 01:03:05.740
of people who somehow

01:03:05.740 --> 01:03:07.960
they're appointed or self-appointed

01:03:07.960 --> 01:03:11.260
legal authorities

01:03:11.260 --> 01:03:12.100
so

01:03:12.100 --> 01:03:14.540
that point I think of the Joseph Kaur is very

01:03:14.540 --> 01:03:16.540
important. We should have a Jewish

01:03:16.540 --> 01:03:18.500
code. Second,

01:03:19.320 --> 01:03:20.560
the Jewish code should

01:03:20.560 --> 01:03:22.600
not reflect one single

01:03:22.600 --> 01:03:23.420
Jewish community.

01:03:24.980 --> 01:03:26.220
But should be reflect

01:03:26.220 --> 01:03:28.280
all of Jewish communities.

01:03:29.000 --> 01:03:30.220
In Jewish communities sometimes they should

01:03:30.220 --> 01:03:31.960
compromise among themselves.

01:03:32.900 --> 01:03:34.500
Yes? So I'm not going to have

01:03:34.500 --> 01:03:35.740
my feeling the way I want it.

01:03:36.360 --> 01:03:38.400
Now I compromise my feeling because of you.

01:03:38.400 --> 01:03:40.320
You compromise in the talents because of me.

01:03:40.780 --> 01:03:41.680
That's the way it is.

01:03:42.100 --> 01:03:44.780
We have to make some sort of compromise, arrangements.

01:03:45.420 --> 01:03:49.480
And these two points, I believe, are of great value.

01:03:50.260 --> 01:03:54.800
Last but not least, I hope that one day, while we're still alive,

01:03:55.860 --> 01:04:00.060
we should renew the whole ideal of the smicha.

01:04:00.060 --> 01:04:10.060
We have a proper Jewish Sanhedrin, representing all Jewish traditions and ideologies.

01:04:10.060 --> 01:04:15.120
and together they should decide what Jewish law is all about.

01:04:17.580 --> 01:04:18.460
Thank you.

01:04:21.700 --> 01:04:26.640
Professor, didn't the reliance of the Orthodox upon the Shulchan Aruch

01:04:26.640 --> 01:04:33.200
create the stagnation where the Orthodox would not make any new amendments

01:04:33.200 --> 01:04:35.900
as had been going on for thousands of years?

01:04:35.900 --> 01:04:41.220
and didn't that stimulate the creation of the reform and conservative movements?

01:04:41.720 --> 01:04:43.120
Well, let me respond to you.

01:04:43.120 --> 01:04:47.900
One of the early articles that are written by me when I came to this country

01:04:47.900 --> 01:04:50.520
was to show that in the Sephardic tradition,

01:04:52.280 --> 01:04:58.640
they circumvent, developed the points of the Shukah Aruch constantly.

01:04:59.120 --> 01:05:02.060
Forty years after the Shukah Aruch, there were already developments,

01:05:03.180 --> 01:05:05.200
and very significant developments.

01:05:05.900 --> 01:05:14.220
And you'll find, paradoxically, the greatest growth in Jewish legal literature

01:05:14.220 --> 01:05:19.060
comes from the Sephardic traditions, specifically from those communities

01:05:19.060 --> 01:05:22.780
in which the Shulchan Aruch was considered as legally binding.

01:05:23.420 --> 01:05:29.340
Shulchan Aruch is a kind of a generative kind of work in which generates more knowledge.

01:05:29.340 --> 01:05:38.040
The reason why certain segments were stagnant is because they wanted to be stagnant.

01:05:38.960 --> 01:05:52.280
And they used the Shulchan Aruch, or what have you, as pretext to hide away from reality and to prevent Jewish progress.

01:05:52.280 --> 01:05:54.700
the Shukran Aruch himself

01:05:54.700 --> 01:05:56.320
in his own responsa

01:05:56.320 --> 01:05:58.360
very intelligently

01:05:58.360 --> 01:06:00.900
departs in many cases

01:06:00.900 --> 01:06:01.820
from the Shukran Aruch

01:06:01.820 --> 01:06:04.080
because from the time that he wrote the Shukran Aruch

01:06:04.080 --> 01:06:06.900
until the time the responsa came to his desk

01:06:06.900 --> 01:06:09.640
some time had lapsed

01:06:09.640 --> 01:06:11.160
and already he was ready

01:06:11.160 --> 01:06:13.260
and he did make changes

01:06:13.260 --> 01:06:15.340
Nazar Melvedek has another book

01:06:15.340 --> 01:06:16.420
which I did not mention

01:06:16.420 --> 01:06:18.000
it's called Bedek Abayit

01:06:18.000 --> 01:06:21.140
in which he makes the final revisions

01:06:21.140 --> 01:06:22.380
right before he dies.

01:06:23.180 --> 01:06:24.960
So a great legal mind

01:06:24.960 --> 01:06:27.460
is constantly evolving.

01:06:28.160 --> 01:06:29.280
The Shulchan Arush is supposed to be

01:06:29.280 --> 01:06:30.180
a pattern

01:06:30.180 --> 01:06:33.040
that you could accept

01:06:33.040 --> 01:06:35.520
and as a challenge

01:06:35.520 --> 01:06:37.000
try to improve.

01:06:37.180 --> 01:06:39.360
And if you improve, all the best

01:06:39.360 --> 01:06:40.240
and all the better.

01:06:41.260 --> 01:06:43.260
The reason why there is

01:06:43.260 --> 01:06:44.560
a stagnation in

01:06:44.560 --> 01:06:47.020
Jewish legal

01:06:47.020 --> 01:06:49.320
thought, it is not

01:06:49.320 --> 01:06:56.320
because the Jewish legal system demands stagnation, but rather because those who proclaim themselves

01:06:56.960 --> 01:07:03.960
as the spokesmen for the legal system want to be stagnant.

01:07:06.320 --> 01:07:11.320
Thank you very much. Oh, that's it.

01:07:11.320 --> 01:07:16.320
Bedeq habayt. Bedeq habayt.

01:07:17.160 --> 01:07:17.440
Thank you.

01:07:19.320 --> 01:07:20.320
Yes.

01:07:20.320 --> 01:07:21.320
Two years ago, I was in Krakow.

01:07:21.320 --> 01:07:22.320
Yes.

01:07:22.320 --> 01:07:23.320
In fact, I have a entire collection with my cemetery.

01:07:23.320 --> 01:07:24.320
There's also a cemetery.

01:07:24.320 --> 01:07:25.320
The cemetery was devastated during the war.

01:07:25.320 --> 01:07:26.320
And I heard a very charming legend told by the presence of the Jewish community.

01:07:26.320 --> 01:07:27.320
It says, the Gestapo members of the Jewish community, they were the ones who were the

01:07:27.320 --> 01:07:28.320
most powerful in the world.

01:07:28.320 --> 01:07:29.320
And they were the ones who were the most powerful in the world.

01:07:29.320 --> 01:07:30.320
And they were the ones who were the most powerful in the world.

01:07:30.320 --> 01:07:31.320
And they were the ones who were the most powerful in the world.

01:07:31.320 --> 01:07:32.320
And they were the ones who were the most powerful in the world.

01:07:32.320 --> 01:07:33.320
And they were the ones who were the most powerful in the world.

01:07:33.320 --> 01:07:34.320
And they were the ones who were the most powerful in the world.

01:07:34.320 --> 01:07:35.320
And they were the ones who were the most powerful in the world.

01:07:35.320 --> 01:07:36.820
I have an entire collection with my son.

01:07:36.820 --> 01:07:37.880
There's also a cemetery.

01:07:37.880 --> 01:07:41.460
The cemetery was devastated during the war.

01:07:41.460 --> 01:07:44.860
And I heard a very, very charming legend

01:07:44.860 --> 01:07:47.560
told by the presence of the Jewish community.

01:07:47.560 --> 01:07:51.840
It says the Gestapo man who forced some people

01:07:51.840 --> 01:07:55.420
to wreck all the stones and they reseal it

01:07:55.420 --> 01:07:57.880
and everything else, only then it came to the last

01:07:57.880 --> 01:07:58.720
labor of the war.

01:07:58.720 --> 01:08:02.760
And the responsible Gestapo commander

01:08:02.760 --> 01:08:06.360
He came almost like he says, he followed a religion.

01:08:06.360 --> 01:08:08.200
He says, don't do it, don't torture, torture.

01:08:08.200 --> 01:08:09.760
That mystical force.

01:08:09.760 --> 01:08:12.880
And this is the only grave remaining there.

01:08:12.880 --> 01:08:14.000
I have a slide there.

01:08:14.000 --> 01:08:15.140
It's very interesting.

